# zeta-unicode -- name derivation rules (generated by mk_rules.py from
# approach #6's mining run; see INTEGRATION.md for the grammar and the
# build that consumes it).  Every name covered here is CONSTRUCTED from its
# code point at build time and is absent from the compressed streams; the
# build verifies each one byte-for-byte against data/DerivedName.txt.
@unicode 18.0.0
@corpus 35351
@derived 6677
@arms 5286
@atoms 324
@stream plen delta8 10 1
@stream slen raw 4 1
@stream mids raw 16 16
@runs 4 1
@patterns 4 1

# --- atoms: one space-delimited token each (`A<id:04d> <token>`).  A token ends
#     in the space it carries; a final token with no trailing space is
#     written without one.  The token is what the generated tree pushes.
# --- arms: one per line, sorted by code point: `<cp_lo>[:<cp_hi>] <recipe>`
#     recipe = push-atom codes and exactly one hole:
#        <atom>            one letter, or `'<letter>` / `''<l><l>` for ids >= 52
#        +<n> / -<n>       hole: push the byte (cp - cp_lo + n), decimal, signed
#        =<hex>[,<width>]  hole: push uppercase hex of (cp - cp_lo + <hex>),
#                          zero-padded to <width> (absent = no padding)
#     A hole's value is stated relative to the arm's first code point, which is
#     what keeps these numbers short; the build turns it back into an offset.

